      "title": "Immutability and the String Pool: The Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Immutability and the String Pool: The Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Immutable Strings",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Immutable== = state fixed after construction",
                "`concat`, `replace`, `toUpperCase`, `trim` return a **NEW** String",
                "Original stays untouched: `s.trim();` alone is lost",
                "`final` class, private value: nobody can subclass or mutate",
                "Gives thread-safe use, cached hash (HashMap key), safe paths"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The String Pool",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Pool== = JVM-wide table of unique literals, on the heap",
                "Literal reuses the pooled object: `\"a\" == \"a\"` is true",
                "`new String(\"a\")` = separate heap object, outside the pool",
                "`intern()` returns the pooled instance"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "String a = \"a\";",
                "String n = new String(\"a\");",
                "System.out.println(a == n);",
                "System.out.println(n.intern() == a);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "false",
                "true"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Constants vs Runtime",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Expression",
                "==",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`\"a\" + \"b\" == \"ab\"`",
                  "{green:true}",
                  "folded at compile time, pooled"
                ],
                [
                  "`x + \"b\" == \"ab\"` (non-final `x`)",
                  "{red:false}",
                  "runtime concat, new object"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "`==` compares references, `equals()` compares content. Always assign the result: `s = s.trim()`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "equals vs == and Comparing Strings",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "equals vs == and Comparing Strings",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. == vs equals()",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`==` compares ==references==: same object?",
                "`equals()` compares ==content==",
                "For Strings you almost always want `equals()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "String s1 = \"hi\", s2 = \"hi\";",
                "String s3 = new String(\"hi\");",
                "System.out.println(s1 == s2);",
                "System.out.println(s1 == s3);",
                "System.out.println(s1.equals(s3));"
              ],
              "note": "literals share one pooled object; new String makes another"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "true",
                "false",
                "true"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Null-safe and ordering",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Gives",
                "Use when"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`\"admin\".equals(input)`",
                  "boolean",
                  "literal first: no {red:NullPointerException}"
                ],
                [
                  "`Objects.equals(a, b)`",
                  "boolean",
                  "both may be null"
                ],
                [
                  "`equalsIgnoreCase(s)`",
                  "boolean",
                  "case-insensitive content"
                ],
                [
                  "`a.compareTo(b)`",
                  "negative / 0 / positive",
                  "sorting, lexicographic by char value"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. equals needs hashCode",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Override `equals` ==and== `hashCode` together",
                "Equal objects must have ==equal hash codes==",
                "`HashMap` and `HashSet` find the bucket by hash first"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Silent failure",
              "text": "Override only `equals` and an equal key hashes to another bucket: `get` and `contains` return **null / false** with no error."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "StringBuilder and Efficient String Building",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "StringBuilder and Efficient String Building",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What StringBuilder Is",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Mutable== char sequence with an internal **resizable buffer**",
                "`append`, `insert`, `delete`, `reverse`, `setCharAt` change it ==in place==",
                "Each returns `this`, so calls can be **chained**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Builder vs Concatenation",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:`+=` in a loop} makes a new String every pass: ==O(n^2)== copying",
                "{green:One builder}: `append` in the loop, `toString()` once at the end"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "String",
                "StringBuilder",
                "StringBuffer"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Mutable",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "{green:Yes}",
                  "{green:Yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "Thread-safe",
                  "Yes (immutable)",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "Yes (synchronized)"
                ],
                [
                  "Use",
                  "Fixed text",
                  "**Default choice**",
                  "Rarely needed"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and Tips",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Chain gives `\"1a\"`: append, append, reverse",
                "Known length? **Pre-size** with `new StringBuilder(capacity)` to avoid regrowth"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "String s = new StringBuilder(16)",
                ".append(\"a\").append(1)",
                ".reverse().toString();",
                "System.out.println(s);"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "1a"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Only in loops",
              "text": "A single `a + b + c` is already ==optimized by the compiler==. Delimited lists: `String.join` or `Collectors.joining`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
