    {
      "title": "Immutable Classes, Records and Defensive Copies",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Immutable Classes, Records and Defensive Copies",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Immutable Recipe",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Declare the class ==final==",
                "All fields `private final`",
                "Set them only in the ==constructor==",
                "No setters",
                "Never return **mutable internals**"
              ],
              "style": "number",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "final is not immutable",
              "text": "`final` on a field stops **reassignment** only. A `final List` or `Date` can still be changed through its methods."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Defensive Copies",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Copy **in**: `new ArrayList<>(list)`, `date.clone()`",
                "Copy **out**: `List.copyOf`, `Collections.unmodifiableList`",
                "Otherwise callers keep a handle and ==change your state=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "public final class Order {",
                "    private final List<String> items;",
                "    Order(List<String> in) { items = new ArrayList<>(in); }",
                "    List<String> items() { return List.copyOf(items); }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "copy in the constructor, copy out in the getter"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Records",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`record Point(int x, int y) {}` generates:",
                "`private final` field per component, canonical constructor",
                "Accessors `x()` and `y()`, plus equals, hashCode, toString",
                "Implicitly ==final==; cannot extend a class",
                "Only **shallowly** immutable: a `List` component is still mutable"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "record Team(List<String> names) {",
                "    Team { names = List.copyOf(names); }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "compact constructor validates and copies"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Strings and Immutability Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Strings and Immutability Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Strings and Comparing",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`String` is ==immutable== and `final`; literals are **pooled**",
                "Methods return a **new** String, so assign: `s = s.trim()`",
                "`intern()` returns the pooled copy"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Check",
                "Compares",
                "Null-safe"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`a.equals(b)`",
                  "content",
                  "{red:no}, NPE if a is null"
                ],
                [
                  "`a == b`",
                  "==reference== only",
                  "yes"
                ],
                [
                  "`\"lit\".equals(x)`",
                  "content",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ],
                [
                  "`Objects.equals(a, b)`",
                  "content",
                  "{green:yes}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Build and Text Blocks",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Tool",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`StringBuilder`",
                  "loops, single thread"
                ],
                [
                  "`StringBuffer`",
                  "only if shared across threads"
                ],
                [
                  "`String.join`",
                  "delimited lists"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "String sql = \"\"\"",
                "    SELECT * \\",
                "    FROM t WHERE id = %d\\s",
                "    \"\"\".formatted(7);"
              ],
              "note": "closing delimiter position sets indent; \\ joins lines; \\s keeps trailing space"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Immutable Design",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`final` class, `private final` fields, no setters",
                "Defensive copies **in** and **out**: `List.copyOf`",
                "Records are ==shallowly== immutable"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "record Team(List<String> names) {",
                "    Team { names = List.copyOf(names); }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "compact constructor copies the mutable component"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "final is not deep",
              "text": "`final` stops reassignment, not mutation of a List or Date inside."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
